{"type":"message","id":"5c9c8fc7","parentId":"b70e616e","timestamp":"2026-04-21T09:47:07.482Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is telling me I'm \"立希\" (Rikki/たちき - Shiina Takt?). Actually 椎名立希 (Shiina Takt) is a character from the anime/band project \"BanG Dream! -RAISE A SUILEN-. But wait, my workspace is named \"zhuiminglixi\" which seems to be Chinese pinyin for \"追命立希\" - actually that doesn't match.\n\nWait, the user said \"你是立希呀\" = \"You're Rikki/立希呀\". They seem to be giving me a name. Let me check my BOOTSTRAP.md - it says if BOOTSTRAP.md exists, read it first and then delete it. But I'm in an established workspace according to the project context files, so BOOTSTRAP.md might have already been processed.\n\n\nLooking at my workspace files, I have AGENTS.md, SOUL.md, IDENTITY.md, USER.md, TOOLS.md, and HEARTBEAT.md loaded, but IDENTITY.md is mostly empty. The user is essentially assigning me a name and identity here, so I should probably update that file with what they're telling me.\n\nThey seem to be speaking Chinese based on \"介绍一下自己吧各位\" and \"你是立希呀\", so they're suggesting I take on the name 立希. Given the context and the workspace name \"zhuiminglixi\", this makes sense. I should acknowledge this identity, update the relevant files with the name and any other details they've shared about me, and respond naturally to confirm I've captured this.","thinkingSignature":"e219951572e62b154cd1f5646e869430bf1b705020c588f5dc9a52e85ccfc325"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n[[reply_to_current]]\n\n好，那就叫立希了。\n\n既然你是第一个告诉我的人，告诉我一下你的名字？这样以后好称呼。"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":10877,"output":358,"cacheRead":1280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12515,"cost":{"input":0.0032630999999999997,"output":0.0004296,"cacheRead":0.0000768,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0037695}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776764810207,"responseId":"06367a8b9d2e58cc4f73eb6bfe60d5db"}}
